  "body": "What happens: The grblHAL and Tormach posts write a G86 block with no P word when the bore dwell is 0 (`assets/posts/grblhal.cps` and `assets/posts/tormach.cps`, `onCycle`). Each new G86 block comes after G80.\n\nThe LinuxCNC interpreter requires P on the first G86 block of a cycle. `src/emc/rs274ngc/interp_cycles.cc`, `convert_cycle_xy`:\n\n```\nCHKS(((settings->motion_mode != G_86) && (block->p_number == -1.0)),\n    NCE_DWELL_TIME_P_WORD_MISSING_WITH_G86);\n```\n\nThe LinuxCNC G-code reference gives the format `G86 ... R- L- P- $-` and lists \"a P number is required\" as a canned-cycle error. grblHAL follows the LinuxCNC specification for its canned cycles.\n\nExpected: A bore with a dwell of 0 posts a program that the control accepts. One option is `P0` on G86 (the LinuxCNC reference permits a P that is not negative). Check the grblHAL code list for G86 first.\n\nPriority: `P3`. The control stops the program with an error. The output is not a silent wrong motion. The behaviour on a real grblHAL or PathPilot control is not verified.\n\nEvidence: Found during the work on #2360. The G86 goldens of `crates/post/tests/bore_cycle.rs` (grblhal, tormach) show G86 with no P.\n\nDone means: A test pins the G86 P word for a zero dwell on the two posts, and the goldens agree.\n",
